1
00:01:50,159 --> 00:01:51,200
The reason I came today

2
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:53,799
is to have you judge who's right.

3
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:54,799
It's about my eldest nephew.

4
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:56,959
When I was heading over,

5
00:01:56,959 --> 00:01:58,040
he was at Yang Er's shop,

6
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,280
trying to sell off our family crew!

7
00:01:59,280 --> 00:01:59,879
That's right, old man!

8
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:00,719
I can testify to that.

9
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:01,480
Selling it right in front of me!

10
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:02,400
Yang Er named a price,

11
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:03,239
and I saw it all with my own eyes!

12
00:02:03,239 --> 00:02:03,760
Ma Laibu,

13
00:02:04,239 --> 00:02:06,079
you aren't picky at all about selling it!

14
00:02:06,159 --> 00:02:08,360
You'd sell it to any Tom, Dick, or Harry!

15
00:02:08,439 --> 00:02:10,080
Those who know say it's a demolition.

16
00:02:10,439 --> 00:02:12,280
Those who don't would think our Ma family

17
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:14,000
is wrecking the shrine and digging graves!

18
00:02:14,879 --> 00:02:16,919
If my sister knew about this in her grave,

19
00:02:16,919 --> 00:02:17,919
she'd rise up and slap you silly!

20
00:02:18,319 --> 00:02:19,319
Ma Laibu, let me tell you,

21
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:21,000
my brother-in-law is bedridden right now,

22
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,759
and things are tough for the crew,

23
00:02:22,919 --> 00:02:24,400
but don't you still have your Uncle Duoxi?

24
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:27,439
Your uncle and your dad

25
00:02:27,439 --> 00:02:29,319
went through life and death together!

26
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,520
In the entire construction crew,

27
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:31,240
besides your dad,

28
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:33,159
Uncle Duoxi knows our crew best!

29
00:02:33,159 --> 00:02:34,680
Hold on a second, Ma Laibu's aunt.

30
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:35,879
You've got it all twisted.

31
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,159
I get what you're trying to say.

32
00:02:37,319 --> 00:02:37,960
As for this construction crew,

33
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,000
our family isn't buying it.

34
00:02:39,199 --> 00:02:40,159
Our own construction crew

35
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:41,159
is already drowning in troubles!

36
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,280
Mainly, we don't have the money for it.

37
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:42,840
You get that?

38
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:44,080
What do you mean, no money?

39
00:02:44,199 --> 00:02:45,800
Who in this village doesn't know

40
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:46,919
you got the demolition payout?

41
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,039
If you claim you're broke,

42
00:02:48,639 --> 00:02:49,240
then in the entire village,

43
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:51,000
who would dare say they have cash?

44
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,479
You've done your homework, Brother Sai.

45
00:02:52,759 --> 00:02:53,439
Let me tell you,

46
00:02:53,599 --> 00:02:55,639
if I had arrived a minute later today...

47
00:02:55,639 --> 00:02:56,479
If it were a good deal,

48
00:02:56,479 --> 00:02:57,639
treating it like a business,

49
00:02:57,919 --> 00:02:59,120
it's bound to lose money!

50
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:00,159
You know what Ma Laibu told me?

51
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:01,639
That their crew is a mess of bad debts!

52
00:03:01,719 --> 00:03:02,240
Their crew—

53
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:03,199
what does he mean by bad debts?

54
00:03:03,439 --> 00:03:03,800
Don't get physical!

55
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,360
Tell me, what do you mean by bad debts?

56
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,800
My dad told me not to hit women!

57
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:07,319
Don't you lay a hand on me!

58
00:03:07,319 --> 00:03:08,439
Today, my brother-in-law

59
00:03:08,439 --> 00:03:10,240
handed the crew's ledgers to me!

60
00:03:10,439 --> 00:03:12,280
Let's lay them out and compare!

61
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:13,280
Let's see whose books are crooked! Wait.

62
00:03:13,599 --> 00:03:14,159
Hold on!

63
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,199
When did my dad ever give you the ledgers?

64
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:19,599
Explain yourself!

65
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:20,400
Move!

66
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:22,599
Dad, look at them.

67
00:03:22,759 --> 00:03:23,919
Nothing's even happened to him yet,

68
00:03:23,919 --> 00:03:25,080
and they're already turning on each other!

69
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:27,080
Can you please use your brain?

70
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:27,879
Think for a second!

71
00:03:27,879 --> 00:03:28,560
Who is Yang Er?

72
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,800
How dare you try to sell to him? You...

73
00:03:30,039 --> 00:03:31,800
Uh, his... his aunt,

74
00:03:31,879 --> 00:03:32,639
his aunt, you...

75
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:34,560
What was your name again?

76
00:03:35,599 --> 00:03:36,240
What's your name again?

77
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,919
Hao Zhihua.

78
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:48,719
Right.

79
00:03:48,719 --> 00:03:49,719
Ma Jiucheng.

80
00:03:49,919 --> 00:03:50,639
My brother-in-law.

81
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:51,759
Guifen, my sister.

82
00:03:51,919 --> 00:03:53,479
Came over to your place for pork knuckle.

83
00:03:53,479 --> 00:03:54,240
Right, ate three of them.

84
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,080
Ate three.

85
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:56,439
I remember now, I remember.

86
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,800
I get what you're getting at.

87
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:00,400
As for you,

88
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:01,520
you came here today

89
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:05,400
because you want me to take over

90
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,319
Old Ma's construction team,

91
00:04:08,199 --> 00:04:08,520
right?

92
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:12,680
Is this...

93
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,319
Old Ma's idea?

94
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:25,920
Brother Duoxi,

95
00:04:27,079 --> 00:04:27,720
if

96
00:04:28,439 --> 00:04:29,600
you're willing,

97
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,399
if you're interested,

98
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:33,680
I think

99
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:35,040
you can just let me know.

100
00:04:35,959 --> 00:04:38,040
I'll talk to my brother-in-law for you.

101
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:39,680
Who's that Yang Er anyway?

102
00:04:39,959 --> 00:04:42,000
After all, our families go back a long way.

103
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:45,160
Look, Auntie,

104
00:04:45,879 --> 00:04:46,959
Old Ma

105
00:04:47,279 --> 00:04:48,160
is still alive and breathing.

106
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,079
Going behind his back

107
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:53,839
to take what he spent half his life on,

108
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,160
wheeling and dealing like this...

109
00:04:56,839 --> 00:04:58,360
If word gets out,

110
00:04:58,759 --> 00:05:02,160
I, Sai Duoxi, couldn't show my face!

111
00:05:04,399 --> 00:05:05,920
Anyway, I've got things to do today.

112
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:07,399
Let's... let's leave it at that.

113
00:05:07,519 --> 00:05:08,079
Hey, Lao San,

114
00:05:08,639 --> 00:05:09,680
see Auntie out for me.

115
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:21,240
Auntie,

116
00:05:21,639 --> 00:05:21,920
Auntie!

117
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:23,000
Listen to me.

118
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:24,680
We really can't sell to Sai Duoxi.

119
00:05:24,759 --> 00:05:25,560
You don't know him.

120
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:26,759
Auntie, Auntie...

121
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:28,839
Why do you have my dad's ledger?

122
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:31,199
Did... did he send you to see Sai Duoxi?

123
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:31,959
Look,

124
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,079
my dad is sick.

125
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:34,480
There's no way he'll beat Yang Er's price.

126
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:34,800
Wait a second.

127
00:05:36,399 --> 00:05:37,160
You're his aunt, right?

128
00:05:37,399 --> 00:05:38,759
Go back and tell Uncle Ma

129
00:05:39,079 --> 00:05:39,720
that you're too late.

130
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,360
It's already sold.

131
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:41,600
And you...

132
00:05:42,079 --> 00:05:43,199
I'll take you to Yang Er's in a bit

133
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:44,199
to get that paperwork signed.

134
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,120
Let me tell you why.

135
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:47,839
Never do business with close friends.

136
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,120
The accounts always get messy.

137
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:50,319
If the price is too high,

138
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:51,439
my family won't agree.

139
00:05:51,639 --> 00:05:52,480
If the price is too low,

140
00:05:52,759 --> 00:05:54,000
it'll hurt the bond between our families.

141
00:05:54,199 --> 00:05:55,360
Look, the old man and Uncle Ma

142
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:57,000
grew up together like brothers.

143
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:59,279
Inside, the old man said everything

144
00:05:59,519 --> 00:06:00,560
he could and should say.

145
00:06:01,079 --> 00:06:01,839
As for what he couldn't say,

146
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:02,920
I'll say it for him.

147
00:06:03,319 --> 00:06:04,160
I don't know if your coming here

148
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,279
was Uncle Ma's idea,

149
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:06,319
but in my opinion,

150
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:08,040
you shouldn't have come.

151
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:27,600
Is there something on my face?

152
00:06:29,839 --> 00:06:30,439
Nothing at all.

153
00:06:31,639 --> 00:06:32,639
Then what are you staring at?

154
00:06:36,959 --> 00:06:37,600
What's your name?

155
00:06:38,319 --> 00:06:39,079
The third Sai brother.

156
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:40,240
Sai Xiuhe.

157
00:06:40,839 --> 00:06:41,839
You're pretty handsome.

158
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:43,360
Don't hang out with Laibu.

159
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:44,199
He's a deadbeat.

160
00:07:00,639 --> 00:07:03,000
Fresh grilled gluten and skewers!

161
00:07:04,079 --> 00:07:05,240
Steamed buns, stuffed buns!

162
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:05,920
Give me a bag of this.

163
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:06,800
Spicy soup!

164
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:07,560
Coming right up!

165
00:07:09,839 --> 00:07:11,759
Mantis shrimp, conch! All fresh and alive!

166
00:07:11,759 --> 00:07:12,560
Fresh seafood!

167
00:07:12,759 --> 00:07:13,360
Just caught today!

168
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:15,279
Crabs and octopus too, take a look!

169
00:07:16,839 --> 00:07:18,040
Freshly butchered chicken!

170
00:07:18,439 --> 00:07:19,920
Fresh pineapples!

171
00:07:20,279 --> 00:07:21,519
Braised offal, right out of the pot!

172
00:07:21,519 --> 00:07:22,439
Pork cracklings!

173
00:07:22,959 --> 00:07:23,680
Give me two jin of that.

174
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:25,439
Crispy, savory pork cracklings!

175
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:27,160
Here's your cotton candy.

176
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:31,959
Who's home?

177
00:07:31,959 --> 00:07:33,279
I'm back!

178
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:34,800
Qianjin!

179
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:35,240
Auntie, Auntie, Auntie!

180
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,000
Jingran!

181
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:37,439
Sis, Brother-in-law!

182
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:38,480
Happy Mid-Autumn Festival!

183
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:39,319
Happy Mid-Autumn Festival!

184
00:07:39,319 --> 00:07:39,800
Sister-in-law!

185
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:41,000
That's so much stuff!

186
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:42,360
Not really.

187
00:07:42,439 --> 00:07:43,959
It's all from Jingran's hospital.

188
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:45,800
Some are thank-you gifts from patients.

189
00:07:46,639 --> 00:07:47,720
We couldn't finish it all anyway.

190
00:07:48,079 --> 00:07:48,800
You make good money,

191
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:49,680
and barely spend any.

192
00:07:50,199 --> 00:07:51,000
It's all fruit jelly!

193
00:07:51,519 --> 00:07:53,079
Sai Xiuli, hurry up and open this for me!

194
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,439
Why are you so high-maintenance?

195
00:07:55,639 --> 00:07:57,079
Don't let Third Uncle see it later,

196
00:07:57,079 --> 00:07:58,120
or he'll snatch it all away!

197
00:07:58,600 --> 00:07:59,800
Let's go check Dad's emergency medication.

198
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:00,160
Open it.

199
00:08:00,399 --> 00:08:01,000
Xiao Wu!

200
00:08:01,399 --> 00:08:02,439
Xiao Wu! Zhenzhu!

201
00:08:02,519 --> 00:08:03,040
Where are you?

202
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:03,560
Over here, over here!

203
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:03,879
Come out!

204
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:04,319
What is it?

205
00:08:04,319 --> 00:08:05,360
Go pick out the good stuff and bring it inside.

206
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:05,720
Bring what in?

207
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:06,120
Bring what in?

208
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:07,519
Fireworks and firecrackers! Want to set them off?

209
00:08:07,639 --> 00:08:08,199
Yes, let's do it!

210
00:08:08,199 --> 00:08:08,800
Where are they? Outside?

211
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:09,439
Where, where, where?

212
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:09,839
Hurry!

213
00:08:09,839 --> 00:08:10,920
Put them on the second floor! On the second floor!

214
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:16,319
Sister-in-law.

215
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:23,199
Sister-in-law.

216
00:08:25,279 --> 00:08:26,879
Who sets off fireworks for Mid-Autumn?

217
00:08:26,879 --> 00:08:27,879
Where'd that rule come from?

218
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:29,519
What's so weird about that?

219
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,000
People eat dumplings on National Day,

220
00:08:31,439 --> 00:08:32,879
so what's wrong with fireworks on Mid-Autumn?

221
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:34,399
Sister-in-law.

222
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:35,879
I've been thinking.

223
00:08:36,519 --> 00:08:37,320
About this matter...

224
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,600
Us scheming alone won't do any good.

225
00:08:40,039 --> 00:08:41,440
The old man has to make the final call.

226
00:08:41,799 --> 00:08:42,480
Listen to me.

227
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:43,840
That's why,

228
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,360
we stick to our original plan.

229
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:46,440
Today,

230
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:47,720
I'll bring it up, and you back me up.

231
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,799
We'll lay it all out at the dinner table.

232
00:08:49,799 --> 00:08:50,679
What plan?

233
00:08:51,799 --> 00:08:52,440
Sai Laosan,

234
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:54,159
on a day meant for family reunion,

235
00:08:55,039 --> 00:08:55,879
are you trying to tear this house apart?

236
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:03,600
We already got this one.

237
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:06,159
This one, this one!

238
00:09:06,159 --> 00:09:06,639
Second Brother!

239
00:09:06,759 --> 00:09:07,600
What are you two doing here?

240
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:08,240
Second Uncle! Second Sister-in-law!

241
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:09,000
Xiuli!

242
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:09,679
We're buying fireworks.

243
00:09:09,679 --> 00:09:10,600
Second Aunt!

244
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:11,720
Third Brother said he'd buy us some fireworks.

245
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:13,080
Second Aunt, you're so pretty!

246
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,960
I saw you on TV the other day!

247
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,039
It's fine. Third Brother is paying anyway.

248
00:09:16,039 --> 00:09:16,960
I'll take you to a live taping next time.

249
00:09:17,799 --> 00:09:19,159
Pick... pick fewer.

250
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:19,759
Okay.

251
00:09:20,679 --> 00:09:21,120
Hold this for me.

252
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:22,679
Let's go.

253
00:09:23,039 --> 00:09:23,840
I want two of these.

254
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:26,759
Tonight is a good opportunity.

255
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:28,080
With so many people around,

256
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,320
your dad won't do anything to you.

257
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:32,919
We'll see.

258
00:09:33,519 --> 00:09:34,240
Wen Jiayin.

259
00:09:34,799 --> 00:09:35,799
Didn't you come into my room...

260
00:09:35,919 --> 00:09:36,879
You... Didn't you come to my room

261
00:09:36,879 --> 00:09:37,279
and tell me—

262
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:38,480
Eldest Sister-in-law!

263
00:09:38,679 --> 00:09:39,679
Happy holidays!

264
00:09:39,799 --> 00:09:40,639
Meifan!

265
00:09:41,039 --> 00:09:41,879
Long time no see.

266
00:09:41,879 --> 00:09:43,080
Long time no see!

267
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,039
You look great.

268
00:09:44,039 --> 00:09:44,720
Your sweater is so pretty.

269
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:46,039
What were you two scheming just now?

270
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:49,720
Scheming against you, of course.

271
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:51,799
Everyone in our family is dirt-poor except you.

272
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:52,919
Who else would we target?

273
00:09:53,279 --> 00:09:54,639
Eldest Sister-in-law, thanks for today.

274
00:09:54,639 --> 00:09:55,519
Cooking for the whole family...

275
00:09:55,519 --> 00:09:56,799
It's just as good as a hotel chef's!

276
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:59,399
It's nothing. Isn't it like this every year?

277
00:09:59,399 --> 00:10:00,159
I'm used to it.

278
00:10:00,159 --> 00:10:01,279
Come on, come in.

279
00:10:01,279 --> 00:10:02,919
Give it to me! I want the big one!

280
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,000
Second Sister-in-law!

281
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:05,519
I missed you so much!

282
00:10:06,679 --> 00:10:08,720
Your new perm looks so gorgeous.

283
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,159
Where'd you get these earrings? They're stunning.

284
00:10:10,159 --> 00:10:11,320
They're really trendy right now.

285
00:10:11,399 --> 00:10:12,039
I'll take you to buy a pair.

286
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:12,639
Awesome!

287
00:10:12,639 --> 00:10:14,159
That store has so much cool stuff.

288
00:10:14,159 --> 00:10:15,519
You'll definitely find a lot of great stuff.

289
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:16,720
Have a seat.

290
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:17,720
The mooncakes I sent you the other day,

291
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:18,559
did you eat them yet?

292
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:19,600
I did.

293
00:10:19,679 --> 00:10:20,559
Egg yolk and shredded coconut.

294
00:10:21,559 --> 00:10:21,919
Where's Dad?

295
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:23,240
Dad went to the hospital.

296
00:10:23,799 --> 00:10:24,679
Isn't today Mid-Autumn Festival?

297
00:10:24,919 --> 00:10:25,720
He went to visit Uncle Ma.

298
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:27,600
Meifan is here too.

299
00:10:27,879 --> 00:10:28,399
What a rare sight.

300
00:10:29,799 --> 00:10:30,919
Everyone is here today.

301
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,360
About Dad being sick,

302
00:10:32,679 --> 00:10:33,559
shouldn't we take this chance

303
00:10:33,559 --> 00:10:34,679
to talk it over with everyone?

304
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:35,559
We definitely can't bring that up.

305
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,200
Didn't we already agree?

306
00:10:38,159 --> 00:10:38,799
If the old man doesn't mention it,

307
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:39,879
we all pretend we don't know.

308
00:10:40,879 --> 00:10:41,960
But when it comes to health,

309
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:42,799
money is trivial.

310
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:43,879
I think we can talk about it.

311
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:44,799
You make the call.

312
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:53,000
Director Jin,

313
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:55,840
do you have some thoughts on this too?

314
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:08,120
Here we are.

315
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:08,519
This one.

316
00:11:08,679 --> 00:11:09,080
Right, right, right.

317
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:09,639
It's right here.

318
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,279
Easy, easy, careful.

319
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:12,840
Old Ma.

320
00:11:14,879 --> 00:11:16,039
There you are, old pals.

321
00:11:17,039 --> 00:11:18,240
Put it on the windowsill. Right over there.

322
00:11:19,759 --> 00:11:20,159
Dacheng.

323
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:23,879
Xi knows me best!

324
00:11:23,879 --> 00:11:24,480
Come on, come on.

325
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:24,960
Here, here.

326
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:25,679
Use this one. Use this.

327
00:11:25,679 --> 00:11:26,440
Paper cups are right here.

328
00:11:26,679 --> 00:11:27,399
Pour it in these.

329
00:11:27,759 --> 00:11:29,039
Paper cups for liquor?

330
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:29,720
Here, here.

331
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:30,440
Got 'em, brought real glasses.

332
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,080
Take these.

333
00:11:32,919 --> 00:11:34,480
You really thought of everything!

334
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:37,720
Do you think this money...

335
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:38,639
...will I get a cut?

336
00:11:39,919 --> 00:11:41,799
Getting a cut or not is one thing.

337
00:11:41,799 --> 00:11:42,639
Whether you actually want it...

338
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,360
...is another story entirely.

339
00:11:45,679 --> 00:11:47,480
All I know is Qianjin's registered here.

340
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:48,720
How much you get...

341
00:11:49,279 --> 00:11:50,720
...is strictly between you siblings.

342
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:51,639
It's none of my business.

343
00:11:54,519 --> 00:11:55,600
Second Brother, I need to talk to you.

344
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:56,759
What are you two plotting?

345
00:11:56,759 --> 00:11:57,600
Let's go. We'll talk outside.

346
00:11:58,279 --> 00:11:59,080
Let's find somewhere quiet.

347
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:06,200
I've made up my mind for tonight.

348
00:12:08,159 --> 00:12:08,639
Let's head inside.

349
00:12:15,159 --> 00:12:16,240
Second Brother, listen to me.

350
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,279
Everyone's here today.

351
00:12:17,759 --> 00:12:19,039
After the toast, I'll bring up dividing the money.

352
00:12:19,039 --> 00:12:19,519
Back me up.

353
00:12:19,519 --> 00:12:20,519
You can't bring it up today.

354
00:12:21,399 --> 00:12:22,279
Why the hell not?

355
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:24,000
Wen Jiayin and I already worked it out.

356
00:12:25,159 --> 00:12:26,440
What do you mean you two worked it out?

357
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:27,840
What exactly did you agree on?

358
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:29,559
Wen Jiayin talked to me two days ago.

359
00:12:29,679 --> 00:12:30,840
Do you know how much her proposal asked?

360
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,519
I don't care what proposal she pitched you.

361
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,360
Bottom line, you cannot bring it up today.

362
00:12:34,559 --> 00:12:35,279
If you dare mention it...

363
00:12:35,279 --> 00:12:36,320
...don't blame me for humiliating you!

364
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,720
Like hell I'm showing you any respect!

365
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:47,279
You haven't even cleaned up your own shit!

366
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:49,200
Just remember not to bring it up today!

367
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:50,200
Listen to me first.

368
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,000
Stop making such a fuss!

369
00:12:51,639 --> 00:12:52,000
Lao'er.

370
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,159
I bought you a lipstick.

371
00:12:56,679 --> 00:12:57,840
I get a gift, too?

372
00:12:57,840 --> 00:13:00,600
Of course! And a bottle of perfume.

373
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,159
Let my mom try some, too!

374
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:02,879
Let my mom try it, too!

375
00:13:02,879 --> 00:13:03,919
Come on, give it to me, give it here!

376
00:13:03,919 --> 00:13:04,559
Here, for your mom.

377
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:05,440
Mom!

378
00:13:05,879 --> 00:13:06,600
Mom, come out for a second!

379
00:13:07,039 --> 00:13:07,360
It looks great.

380
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:07,720
What is it?

381
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:09,000
Come on, hold out your hand.

382
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:11,480
Rub it together and take a sniff.

383
00:13:11,759 --> 00:13:12,279
Smells good, right?

384
00:13:13,320 --> 00:13:14,200
I'm busy working here.

385
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,279
Why spray me with something so fragrant?

386
00:13:16,559 --> 00:13:18,279
Let my mom try the lipstick too, okay?

387
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:19,240
Mom, do you want to try it?

388
00:13:19,399 --> 00:13:20,000
Sure, why not.

389
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:20,759
Zhenzhu,

390
00:13:20,919 --> 00:13:22,159
your Second Aunt rarely visits.

391
00:13:22,159 --> 00:13:22,840
Don't bother her.

392
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:23,480
Go do your homework.

393
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:24,279
It's fine, Sister-in-law.

394
00:13:24,279 --> 00:13:25,720
I finished my homework ages ago!

395
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:27,360
Mom, try it! Try it on!

396
00:13:27,519 --> 00:13:28,120
All right, all right.

397
00:13:28,279 --> 00:13:29,000
I'll... I'll take you upstairs.

398
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,840
Go double-check it, okay?

399
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:31,519
I already finished!

400
00:13:31,679 --> 00:13:32,159
Let's go, come on.

401
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:33,440
I told you, I finished it!

402
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:33,840
Let's go.

403
00:13:34,679 --> 00:13:34,919
Move it.

404
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:36,960
Sister-in-law,

405
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,799
next time I'll bring you some lipsticks.

406
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:41,120
They'll look great on you.

407
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:42,840
No need.

408
00:13:43,519 --> 00:13:44,879
I never use this stuff anyway.

409
00:13:49,759 --> 00:13:50,240
Dacheng.

410
00:13:51,159 --> 00:13:52,519
So, yesterday...

411
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:56,120
Hao... what was her name again?

412
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:57,240
Hao Zhihua.

413
00:13:57,519 --> 00:13:58,080
Right, right.

414
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:00,279
Laijiao's aunt.

415
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,360
What's the deal with that anyway?

416
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:08,080
Her? Oh, her.

417
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,440
Dacheng, if you have something to say,

418
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:13,240
just tell me straight.

419
00:14:13,799 --> 00:14:15,159
Don't beat around the bush.

420
00:14:15,159 --> 00:14:16,720
Sending a girl over here to...

421
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:19,440
Right now, she's the only one in charge.

422
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:21,399
Those two bastard sons of mine,

423
00:14:21,559 --> 00:14:22,639
can I count on either of them?

424
00:14:23,159 --> 00:14:23,440
Right?

425
00:14:25,399 --> 00:14:25,799
Otherwise,

426
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:26,720
why don't you take over?

427
00:14:27,919 --> 00:14:28,360
Me? I...

428
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:28,879
Think you can handle it?

429
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,080
I... No, no way.

430
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:31,480
Xizi.

431
00:14:32,639 --> 00:14:33,759
In all seriousness,

432
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:35,039
why don't we

433
00:14:36,919 --> 00:14:37,720
just merge our two teams?

434
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:38,919
Name your price.

435
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:42,039
As long as it's reasonable, I'm fine with it.

436
00:14:43,519 --> 00:14:43,840
Xizi.

437
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:47,919
I'm short on cash right now.

438
00:14:48,039 --> 00:14:49,440
From your demolition payout...

439
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:51,039
Just whatever you can spare.

440
00:14:51,559 --> 00:14:52,440
Come on, it's a holiday.

441
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,320
Is this really the time to talk about this?

442
00:14:54,679 --> 00:14:56,000
Besides, you're still sick.

443
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:57,240
Focus on recovering first.

444
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:58,600
Once you're back on your feet,

445
00:14:58,600 --> 00:14:59,679
we can take our time and talk.

446
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:00,360
But...

447
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:00,759
Okay?

448
00:15:00,759 --> 00:15:01,639
Fine, forget it, forget it.

449
00:15:01,919 --> 00:15:02,720
Finish this drink.

450
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:04,120
He still has to head back for dinner.

451
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:05,600
What about your two?

452
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:07,039
It's a holiday. Aren't they coming over?

453
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:09,200
Laijiao will be here soon.

454
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,159
As for those two bastards,

455
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:13,480
until they get their hands on the money,

456
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,120
there's no way they're showing up.

457
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:16,919
I told you so.

458
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,799
You talked about dividing assets so early,

459
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:22,159
can you avoid selling the crew now?

460
00:15:22,519 --> 00:15:22,799
You see?

461
00:15:23,279 --> 00:15:25,360
Come on, like your kids are any better?

462
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:27,440
They don't say it, but what do they think?

463
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:28,080
Do you even know?

464
00:15:28,639 --> 00:15:29,600
Let them think whatever they want.

465
00:15:30,399 --> 00:15:31,200
As long as I'm around,

466
00:15:31,919 --> 00:15:32,840
they wouldn't dare bring it up.

467
00:15:33,519 --> 00:15:34,759
Come on, drink up! Drink, drink!

468
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:35,519
Cheers, drink up.

469
00:15:35,759 --> 00:15:36,039
All right.

470
00:15:36,639 --> 00:15:36,960
Here, come on.

471
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,559
Yeah, right here. This one.

472
00:15:40,519 --> 00:15:41,000
Okay.

473
00:15:43,559 --> 00:15:44,120
Careful, careful.

474
00:15:45,559 --> 00:15:46,399
Stand back.

475
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,200
That's so pretty!

476
00:15:49,879 --> 00:15:50,879
That one looks gorgeous!

477
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:53,200
Let me light it! Let me light it!

478
00:15:54,399 --> 00:15:55,159
Watch out.

479
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:56,159
Quick, get back!

480
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,759
The lights of Keqin,

481
00:16:11,919 --> 00:16:13,240
a peaceful home.

482
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,399
This is the Sai family's

483
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,960
last Mid-Autumn Festival in Qingyangli.

484
00:16:21,039 --> 00:16:22,919
Compared to years past,

485
00:16:23,919 --> 00:16:25,799
the only difference this year

486
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:29,399
is the fortune he now holds.

487
00:16:31,559 --> 00:16:33,480
The plan brewing in Sai Duoxi's mind

488
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:35,679
had to be laid out

489
00:16:36,639 --> 00:16:38,200
and discussed with his kids.

490
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:41,600
Don't give Dad beer.

491
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:42,360
Qianjin!

492
00:16:42,759 --> 00:16:43,080
Alright, alright.

493
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,200
It's all seafood. Don't let Dad drink beer.

494
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:44,759
Dad! Dad!

495
00:16:44,759 --> 00:16:45,399
Dad, you're back.

496
00:16:45,679 --> 00:16:46,000
The old man's here.

497
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:46,879
Dad's back! Hurry, hurry!

498
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:47,559
Dad! Dad!

499
00:16:47,559 --> 00:16:48,159
Happy Mid-Autumn Festival!

500
00:16:48,159 --> 00:16:48,799
You're here.

501
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:50,440
Come on.

502
00:16:50,759 --> 00:16:51,360
Let's sit down.

503
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:52,279
Set the dishes out, come on.

504
00:16:52,279 --> 00:16:53,120
There are still dishes coming.

505
00:16:53,559 --> 00:16:54,360
Here, I'll help you, let me help.

506
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:57,320
Dad.

507
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,039
Happy Mid-Autumn Festival!

508
00:17:01,159 --> 00:17:01,440
Dad.

509
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:03,039
Go be happy with your other dad!

510
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:04,920
Wait, no...

511
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:06,240
Dad...

512
00:17:07,119 --> 00:17:07,720
Grandpa!

513
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:08,680
Grandpa!

514
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:09,200
Happy Mid-Autumn Festival!

515
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:10,640
Happy Mid-Autumn Festival!

516
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,200
Louder!

517
00:17:11,279 --> 00:17:12,599
Happy Mid-Autumn Festival!

518
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:14,799
Grandpa, Happy Mid-Autumn Festival!

519
00:17:16,359 --> 00:17:16,920
Happy holidays, happy holidays!

520
00:17:18,119 --> 00:17:19,559
How did I miss seeing you?

521
00:17:19,559 --> 00:17:20,599
Come on in, come in, come in!

522
00:17:22,119 --> 00:17:22,839
Come on, come over here.

523
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:26,359
Today is the fifteenth of the eighth month,

524
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:28,960
and you could say it's our family's

525
00:17:29,359 --> 00:17:30,759
last Mid-Autumn Festival in this village.

526
00:17:31,079 --> 00:17:32,559
With how things are in our village now,

527
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:35,200
many families can't even get together.

528
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:36,519
I feel very lucky

529
00:17:37,799 --> 00:17:38,599
that we didn't end up

530
00:17:39,119 --> 00:17:40,400
like Uncle Ma's family.

531
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:42,119
As of today,

532
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:43,640
our family can still

533
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,720
sit together in one complete piece.

534
00:17:46,079 --> 00:17:47,359
That's all because of Dad.

535
00:17:48,599 --> 00:17:49,440
If it weren't for Dad,

536
00:17:49,839 --> 00:17:50,960
we wouldn't even be a family.

537
00:17:51,359 --> 00:17:52,240
Let's all raise our glasses

538
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:53,759
to wish Dad

539
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:55,799
endless fortune and longevity!

540
00:17:56,160 --> 00:17:56,480
Hear, hear!

541
00:17:58,279 --> 00:18:01,680
And may we brothers stay united,

542
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:03,119
family harmony brings prosperity to all!

543
00:18:03,119 --> 00:18:03,400
Great!

544
00:18:05,039 --> 00:18:07,240
Under Dad's leadership,

545
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:10,039
may everything go smoothly and unite us.

546
00:18:11,759 --> 00:18:12,079
Cheers!

547
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:16,680
Here, Dad.

548
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:18,519
A toast to you.

549
00:18:18,559 --> 00:18:18,799
Dad.

550
00:18:18,799 --> 00:18:19,079
Good!

551
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:20,759
Happy holidays, Happy Mid-Autumn Festival.

552
00:18:20,759 --> 00:18:21,799
Dad, wishing you good health.

553
00:18:21,799 --> 00:18:22,359
Good, good, good.

554
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:30,279
Dad,

555
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:32,240
you start first.

556
00:18:34,839 --> 00:18:36,039
Well said, son.

557
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:38,400
Seeing all of you

558
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:40,440
so happy,

559
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:42,400
and the whole family

560
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,960
sharing a peaceful meal together...

561
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:46,559
It's true happiness.

562
00:18:48,079 --> 00:18:48,880
It's rare.

563
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:52,880
Look at Uncle Ma's family.

564
00:18:54,599 --> 00:18:56,039
Over some property,

565
00:18:58,039 --> 00:18:59,559
they tore the family apart.

566
00:19:00,079 --> 00:19:01,000
As for us,

567
00:19:02,119 --> 00:19:02,920
usually,

568
00:19:03,799 --> 00:19:05,039
we can hardly get everyone together.

569
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:06,839
Today,

570
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:07,880
everyone is here.

571
00:19:08,079 --> 00:19:08,759
And I

572
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:11,440
want to talk to you

573
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:13,440
about our family's assets.

574
00:19:17,079 --> 00:19:18,440
The demolition payout...

575
00:19:18,799 --> 00:19:20,200
Our share came to

576
00:19:20,359 --> 00:19:22,359
14.28 million.

577
00:19:22,759 --> 00:19:23,880
I didn't say anything,

578
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:25,079
but

579
00:19:26,039 --> 00:19:27,200
I figured you all

580
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:28,759
probably already know.

581
00:19:29,119 --> 00:19:29,480
Right?

582
00:19:34,359 --> 00:19:35,319
Number Three told us.

583
00:19:37,799 --> 00:19:38,119
Dad,

584
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:39,640
in any case,

585
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,279
we'll follow your lead.

586
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:42,920
You're the backbone of this family.

587
00:19:42,920 --> 00:19:44,680
If you say split it, we split it.

588
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:45,599
If you say don't split it,

589
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:47,079
we definitely won't.

590
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,079
Today,

591
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:50,240
I just want to hear

592
00:19:50,759 --> 00:19:51,319
what you all think.

593
00:19:51,799 --> 00:19:52,640
Do you want to split it?

594
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:54,079
How do you want to split it?

595
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:55,559
Speak your minds.

596
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:21,160
Dad,

597
00:20:21,640 --> 00:20:23,039
I'm not hungry yet.

598
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:24,480
Can I...

599
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:27,960
go set off some fireworks with Zhenzhu?

600
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:31,200
Sure. Go on.

601
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:33,640
Remember this:

602
00:20:34,599 --> 00:20:35,160
You

603
00:20:35,839 --> 00:20:37,839
are a son of the Sai family.

604
00:20:38,119 --> 00:20:40,160
There's definitely a share in this for you.

605
00:20:40,359 --> 00:20:40,680
Dad,

606
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:42,519
that's not what I meant.

607
00:20:43,119 --> 00:20:44,240
I am a son of the Sai family.

608
00:20:44,799 --> 00:20:45,079
That's right.

609
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:46,640
Let's go!

610
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:47,440
Alright, go on now.

611
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:50,200
Stay safe.

612
00:21:10,039 --> 00:21:11,279
As the eldest brother here,

613
00:21:11,359 --> 00:21:12,160
I'll state my position first.

614
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:13,640
As for our family,

615
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:15,079
we won't take a share.

616
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:16,240
Dad,

617
00:21:16,559 --> 00:21:17,319
that money,

618
00:21:17,599 --> 00:21:18,720
you just keep it for yourself.

619
00:21:20,759 --> 00:21:21,799
What about you, Second Brother?

620
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:30,559
Dad,

621
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,559
whether we get a share doesn't matter.

622
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:34,039
Just arrange it however you see fit.

623
00:21:34,839 --> 00:21:35,480
Actually,

624
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:36,720
today Xiuliang

625
00:21:37,319 --> 00:21:38,599
has something to tell you.

626
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:40,599
Dad is right.

627
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:42,920
Let's lay everything on the table.

628
00:21:46,279 --> 00:21:46,920
What is it?

629
00:21:55,279 --> 00:21:56,359
Dad, I'm going to say it then.

630
00:21:56,559 --> 00:21:57,440
But let's agree on one thing first.

631
00:21:57,759 --> 00:21:58,440
After I say it,

632
00:21:58,799 --> 00:21:59,720
you can't get mad.

633
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:00,839
No losing your temper.

634
00:22:01,519 --> 00:22:02,480
Go ahead and speak.

635
00:22:02,759 --> 00:22:04,880
Everyone sitting here is family.

636
00:22:05,319 --> 00:22:06,640
Just speak your mind.

637
00:22:08,759 --> 00:22:09,319
Actually, about this matter...

638
00:22:09,319 --> 00:22:10,480
Second Brother, I know what you want to say.

639
00:22:10,799 --> 00:22:12,000
You want to bring up Fourth Brother.

640
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:12,400
Right?

641
00:22:12,559 --> 00:22:13,720
Can you let me finish?

642
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:14,119
Second Brother,

643
00:22:14,559 --> 00:22:15,440
you just want to say

644
00:22:15,759 --> 00:22:16,920
that you work at the Port Authority,

645
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:18,680
so you moved Fourth Brother's residency,

646
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:19,400
and you want a bigger cut.

647
00:22:19,839 --> 00:22:20,200
Am I right?

648
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:21,960
We can talk about your issue later.

649
00:22:22,799 --> 00:22:23,640
I get the picture now.

650
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:25,119
Dad's intention is for everyone to get a cut.

651
00:22:25,319 --> 00:22:26,440
Let's address Number Five first.

652
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:28,319
As for Number Five,

653
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:29,680
we raise him till he's 18,

654
00:22:30,119 --> 00:22:30,920
and see him married off.

655
00:22:31,799 --> 00:22:32,519
Fair enough.

656
00:22:33,119 --> 00:22:33,920
But Number Five

657
00:22:34,559 --> 00:22:36,000
isn't a Sai after all.

658
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:38,440
If he gets a share of the money,

659
00:22:38,559 --> 00:22:38,880
I

660
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:40,000
won't agree.

661
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:42,440
As for you, Fourth Brother,

662
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:43,839
if Dad feels bad for you

663
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:45,599
and asks us to pitch in,

664
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,119
that's totally fine.

665
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:47,960
I'd agree to that.

666
00:22:49,680 --> 00:22:51,160
Qianjin's residency has been moved back.

667
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:52,039
Her registered household is here now.

668
00:22:52,160 --> 00:22:53,240
When we talked about moving it back,

669
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:54,359
nobody brought this up, did they?

670
00:22:54,759 --> 00:22:55,920
Without saying a word back then,

671
00:22:56,559 --> 00:22:57,319
what do you take Qianjin for?

672
00:22:58,359 --> 00:22:59,000
A tool?

673
00:22:59,759 --> 00:23:01,160
Enough, Jingran, stop talking.

674
00:23:03,319 --> 00:23:03,680
Fine.

675
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:05,920
Anyway,

676
00:23:06,079 --> 00:23:07,039
I've talked with Eldest Sister-in-law

677
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:08,000
and Second Brother.

678
00:23:08,599 --> 00:23:09,519
Technically speaking,

679
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:11,000
the only ones entitled to the money

680
00:23:11,119 --> 00:23:12,799
are Eldest Brother, Second Brother, and me.

681
00:23:14,039 --> 00:23:14,400
Second Brother,

682
00:23:14,759 --> 00:23:16,160
your residency has already been moved out.

683
00:23:16,440 --> 00:23:17,759
If you take the lion's share,

684
00:23:17,759 --> 00:23:18,599
that really wouldn't be right.

685
00:23:19,359 --> 00:23:20,519
Who does that leave eligible?

686
00:23:20,839 --> 00:23:21,440
Just me and Eldest Brother.

687
00:23:22,119 --> 00:23:22,799
And Eldest Brother

688
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:24,440
is still running your construction team.

689
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:26,400
You have to factor that in.

690
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:27,680
I also heard

691
00:23:28,119 --> 00:23:29,160
you want to live with Second Brother now.

692
00:23:30,079 --> 00:23:31,160
I really don't agree with that.

693
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:33,519
Second Sister-in-law can't care for you.

694
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:34,599
Eldest Sister-in-law doing it makes sense.

695
00:23:34,599 --> 00:23:35,200
Third Brother, you...

696
00:23:35,559 --> 00:23:36,960
Do you even know what you're saying?

697
00:23:37,559 --> 00:23:38,440
Are you even human?

698
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:39,400
Human or not,

699
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:40,599
isn't it the truth?

700
00:23:41,319 --> 00:23:42,480
No one wanted to talk about it, right?

701
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:43,799
Well, today I'm putting it on the table.

702
00:23:43,799 --> 00:23:44,559
Let's lay it all out.

703
00:23:44,559 --> 00:23:45,440
No more guessing games.

704
00:23:47,279 --> 00:23:47,680
Right?

705
00:23:59,000 --> 00:23:59,480
Say something!

706
00:24:01,559 --> 00:24:02,720
Sister-in-law, speak up for me!

707
00:24:03,599 --> 00:24:04,759
Wait, what did we talk about the other day?

708
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:08,519
Go on, light it.

709
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:15,920
This is so much fun!

710
00:24:27,799 --> 00:24:28,440
Wen Jiayin,

711
00:24:28,920 --> 00:24:29,839
you're throwing me under the bus again.

712
00:24:29,839 --> 00:24:31,039
Playing the virtuous daughter-in-law, eh?

713
00:24:31,119 --> 00:24:32,359
Didn't we agree you'd back me up?

714
00:24:32,359 --> 00:24:33,000
Say something!

715
00:24:33,359 --> 00:24:34,599
What did we agree on the other day?

716
00:24:34,599 --> 00:24:35,799
What... what can I say?

717
00:24:35,799 --> 00:24:36,960
What do you want me to say?

718
00:24:37,759 --> 00:24:38,119
Lao San.

719
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:39,799
Fine.

720
00:24:41,519 --> 00:24:41,839
Dad,

721
00:24:43,319 --> 00:24:44,160
Lao San did come to me,

722
00:24:44,359 --> 00:24:45,720
but I don't agree with what he's doing.

723
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:47,359
Still, what Lao San just said

724
00:24:47,559 --> 00:24:48,079
makes sense.

725
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:49,039
Meifan

726
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:50,759
grew up pampered,

727
00:24:50,759 --> 00:24:52,240
she doesn't know how to care for someone.

728
00:24:53,079 --> 00:24:53,720
Unlike me.

729
00:24:54,039 --> 00:24:55,559
I'm used to taking care of people.

730
00:24:56,279 --> 00:24:56,559
Dad,

731
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:59,359
you want to live with Second Brother.

732
00:24:59,799 --> 00:25:00,960
I just can't make peace with that.

733
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:02,599
With all the younger siblings here today,

734
00:25:02,599 --> 00:25:04,039
why not tell me in front of everyone?

735
00:25:04,519 --> 00:25:05,960
Where do you feel I've fallen short?

736
00:25:05,960 --> 00:25:07,599
What... what are my flaws?

737
00:25:07,599 --> 00:25:08,480
Where did I go wrong?

738
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:10,319
Tell me, and I'll change. Okay?

739
00:25:10,319 --> 00:25:11,720
Zhenzhu's mom, Zhenzhu's mom...

740
00:25:12,119 --> 00:25:13,680
Didn't I already tell you?

741
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:15,640
That's not what I meant.

742
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:18,440
It's just that Zhenzhu started 7th grade,

743
00:25:19,200 --> 00:25:20,720
and the child needs to study.

744
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:21,920
If I move in there,

745
00:25:22,319 --> 00:25:23,279
with people coming and going,

746
00:25:23,279 --> 00:25:24,680
wouldn't I just be in the way?

747
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:25,920
You wouldn't be in the way, Dad.

748
00:25:26,200 --> 00:25:27,480
All right, all right, Sister-in-Law.

749
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:28,599
Just drop it.

750
00:25:28,960 --> 00:25:30,519
Dad gave his answer, and that's that.

751
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,720
Why force an explanation out of him?

752
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:35,160
He just wants to live with Second Brother.

753
00:25:35,160 --> 00:25:35,880
Is that a crime?

754
00:25:36,759 --> 00:25:37,279
You want to hear it?

755
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:38,319
What are you doing?

756
00:25:39,400 --> 00:25:39,920
Sister-in-Law,

757
00:25:40,519 --> 00:25:41,759
you're just afraid of people gossiping.

758
00:25:41,759 --> 00:25:42,720
What do you expect Dad to do?

759
00:25:42,799 --> 00:25:43,799
Award you an honor banner?

760
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:46,680
And broadcast it over the loudspeaker?

761
00:25:47,359 --> 00:25:47,720
Second Sister-in-Law,

762
00:25:47,960 --> 00:25:49,079
aren't you a TV host?

763
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:49,799
Why don't we go on— Qianjin!

764
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:50,759
the TV station,

765
00:25:50,880 --> 00:25:52,000
and make a special show for Sister-in-Law?

766
00:25:52,240 --> 00:25:54,000
Talk about how well you treated Dad,

767
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,000
and list all the— Qianjin!

768
00:25:55,279 --> 00:25:56,000
That's quite enough!

769
00:25:56,559 --> 00:25:57,839
How can you talk to your sister-in-law like that?

770
00:25:58,039 --> 00:25:59,160
Is that what Sister-in-Law meant?

771
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:01,720
She genuinely cares about Dad.

772
00:26:02,279 --> 00:26:03,279
She's looked after Dad for so many years,

773
00:26:03,599 --> 00:26:05,079
she's just used to it by now.

774
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:05,799
Fine.

775
00:26:06,039 --> 00:26:06,799
Used to it, right?

776
00:26:06,799 --> 00:26:08,279
Then he stays six months with each family.

777
00:26:08,279 --> 00:26:08,680
How about that?

778
00:26:08,799 --> 00:26:09,920
Sister-in-Law, does that satisfy you?

779
00:26:11,039 --> 00:26:12,279
In other families, kids neglect their parents.

780
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:13,079
In ours, everyone's fighting to take him.

781
00:26:13,079 --> 00:26:14,039
How wonderful!

782
00:26:14,559 --> 00:26:16,319
Qianjin, sometimes I really envy you.

783
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:17,640
You say whatever you want,

784
00:26:17,640 --> 00:26:18,920
never caring what anyone else thinks.

785
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:19,720
Enough!

786
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:21,000
What are we even arguing about?

787
00:26:21,559 --> 00:26:23,079
Is this about where Dad's going to live?

788
00:26:26,279 --> 00:26:26,960
We're here to talk about splitting the money!

789
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:28,039
Don't get sidetracked.

790
00:26:31,279 --> 00:26:31,960
Are you going to say it or not?

791
00:26:33,160 --> 00:26:34,039
If you won't, I will.

792
00:26:35,079 --> 00:26:35,599
Xiuliang.

793
00:26:36,279 --> 00:26:37,400
Now that we've laid it all out,

794
00:26:37,880 --> 00:26:38,880
why don't you make your stance clear?

795
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:39,960
Dad wants to live with you.

796
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:41,400
Do you think it's better if he stays with you,

797
00:26:41,400 --> 00:26:42,079
or stays with us?

798
00:26:42,079 --> 00:26:43,039
Sister-in-law, I think you're being

799
00:26:43,039 --> 00:26:44,279
a bit relentless about this.

800
00:26:44,559 --> 00:26:45,599
Is this really that complicated?

801
00:26:46,119 --> 00:26:47,480
Does it really take this long to discuss?

802
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:48,519
Where Dad wants to live

803
00:26:48,519 --> 00:26:49,640
is entirely up to him.

804
00:26:50,079 --> 00:26:51,359
Even if he stays with us,

805
00:26:51,640 --> 00:26:52,599
whenever you miss him,

806
00:26:52,599 --> 00:26:53,640
you can always visit.

807
00:26:53,839 --> 00:26:55,000
Any holiday or whenever.

808
00:26:55,759 --> 00:26:56,119
What,

809
00:26:56,119 --> 00:26:56,880
Dad wants to live with me,

810
00:26:56,880 --> 00:26:57,519
and that's not allowed?

811
00:26:58,079 --> 00:26:59,720
You can really tell you're educated.

812
00:26:59,720 --> 00:27:01,000
You make everything sound so nice.

813
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:02,680
Xiuliang,

814
00:27:03,160 --> 00:27:03,960
if Dad stays with you,

815
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:05,519
we're not worried.

816
00:27:06,039 --> 00:27:06,920
We have no problem with it.

817
00:27:07,200 --> 00:27:08,960
You and Meifan won't mistreat him.

818
00:27:09,359 --> 00:27:10,279
But have you considered this?

819
00:27:10,279 --> 00:27:11,599
You just started a new company.

820
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:13,400
It's not even up and running yet.

821
00:27:13,559 --> 00:27:15,400
It'll take time before it runs smoothly.

822
00:27:15,400 --> 00:27:16,920
Running the company and caring for Dad,

823
00:27:17,079 --> 00:27:18,200
do you think Dad won't hold you back?

824
00:27:50,400 --> 00:27:52,079
Mom, Mom, got another lighter?

825
00:27:52,440 --> 00:27:53,559
Mom, got another lighter?

826
00:27:54,759 --> 00:27:55,519
The lighter's empty.

827
00:27:55,519 --> 00:27:56,359
Got another lighter?

828
00:28:05,240 --> 00:28:05,680
Right here.

829
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:08,359
Let's go, Zhenzhu. Let's get going.

830
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:16,440
What did you just say?

831
00:28:18,799 --> 00:28:19,400
What's going on?

832
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:24,440
Lao San said it.

833
00:28:25,400 --> 00:28:26,440
Wen Jiayin.

834
00:28:26,559 --> 00:28:28,200
Now you're saying it was me?

835
00:28:28,319 --> 00:28:29,319
You're selling me out now?

836
00:28:29,319 --> 00:28:30,279
What were you thinking?

837
00:28:30,400 --> 00:28:31,160
Now I get it.

838
00:28:31,319 --> 00:28:32,759
You used me as a pawn, didn't you?

839
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:33,559
What are you doing?

840
00:28:38,519 --> 00:28:39,559
What's really going on?

841
00:29:16,160 --> 00:29:16,519
Dad,

842
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:19,359
I'll be honest with you.

843
00:29:19,720 --> 00:29:20,759
We actually came back today

844
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,319
specifically to tell you about this.

845
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:23,960
I just didn't expect her to say it first.

846
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:25,400
But that's fine.

847
00:29:25,759 --> 00:29:26,480
Even if she hadn't,

848
00:29:26,480 --> 00:29:27,160
we would've told you anyway.

849
00:29:27,440 --> 00:29:28,200
As for Xiuliang,

850
00:29:28,519 --> 00:29:29,920
he submitted his resignation

851
00:29:30,359 --> 00:29:31,960
and started his own law firm.

852
00:29:32,599 --> 00:29:34,440
Since he just left a state institution,

853
00:29:34,720 --> 00:29:35,880
he's bound to go through

854
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:37,039
a period of instability.

855
00:29:37,279 --> 00:29:39,319
He was just afraid you'd worry too much,

856
00:29:39,319 --> 00:29:40,359
so he didn't tell you right away.

857
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:42,160
He wanted to wait until everything

858
00:29:42,519 --> 00:29:43,359
settled down

859
00:29:43,559 --> 00:29:44,400
before telling you.

860
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:46,480
Second Brother started a firm?

861
00:29:46,880 --> 00:29:47,599
What are you doing?

862
00:29:47,599 --> 00:29:48,240
Wait, Xiuliang...

863
00:29:48,519 --> 00:29:49,640
You gave up an iron rice bowl—

864
00:29:49,960 --> 00:29:51,079
you quit a secure state job?

865
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:52,240
For something this big,

866
00:29:52,680 --> 00:29:54,359
you should've talked to us first!

867
00:29:55,079 --> 00:29:56,240
When did this happen?

868
00:29:59,640 --> 00:30:00,319
A few days ago.

869
00:30:00,799 --> 00:30:02,799
When did you first get this idea?

870
00:30:04,960 --> 00:30:05,880
Quite a while ago.

871
00:30:15,359 --> 00:30:15,640
Dad,

872
00:30:16,279 --> 00:30:17,440
let me explain.

873
00:30:17,680 --> 00:30:18,799
Meifan and I actually

874
00:30:18,799 --> 00:30:20,599
have a lot of plans for our future

875
00:30:20,680 --> 00:30:22,119
that we haven't shared with you yet.

876
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:23,599
Before,

877
00:30:23,599 --> 00:30:25,039
we were planning to go abroad.

878
00:30:25,839 --> 00:30:26,640
But one thing led to another,

879
00:30:26,640 --> 00:30:27,839
and things got delayed.

880
00:30:28,200 --> 00:30:29,640
We missed the best window of opportunity,

881
00:30:29,640 --> 00:30:30,839
so we decided to stay.

882
00:30:31,400 --> 00:30:32,160
But as you know,

883
00:30:32,160 --> 00:30:33,480
after years of reform and opening up,

884
00:30:33,720 --> 00:30:35,359
China has undergone tremendous changes.

885
00:30:35,359 --> 00:30:36,079
You've seen it yourself.

886
00:30:36,359 --> 00:30:38,200
Every industry is becoming regulated,

887
00:30:38,200 --> 00:30:39,079
and they all need legal services.

888
00:30:39,279 --> 00:30:40,119
I studied law.

889
00:30:40,400 --> 00:30:41,359
I believe in this field,

890
00:30:41,440 --> 00:30:42,799
I can really make a name for myself.

891
00:30:42,920 --> 00:30:44,319
I don't want a job with a predictable end—

892
00:30:44,319 --> 00:30:45,519
Let me ask you one more thing.

893
00:30:46,960 --> 00:30:48,480
Was this your idea,

894
00:30:49,279 --> 00:30:50,480
or was it hers?

895
00:31:02,279 --> 00:31:03,039
Speak up.

896
00:31:03,680 --> 00:31:04,960
Whose idea was it between you two?

897
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:05,720
Dad...

898
00:31:08,240 --> 00:31:09,839
We're husband and wife.

899
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:11,559
It's not about whose idea it was.

900
00:31:11,559 --> 00:31:12,720
We talk things over together.

901
00:31:12,960 --> 00:31:14,200
But honestly, this idea...

902
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:26,839
Dad, what are you doing?

903
00:31:27,279 --> 00:31:29,000
It's just a job. Is it really worth all this?

904
00:31:31,079 --> 00:31:32,079
Family.

905
00:31:32,880 --> 00:31:34,000
Family with who?

906
00:31:35,079 --> 00:31:36,680
Who's family with who?

907
00:31:57,319 --> 00:31:57,559
Go.

908
00:31:58,480 --> 00:31:59,240
Go on!

909
00:32:00,440 --> 00:32:01,359
What are you standing there for?

910
00:32:09,279 --> 00:32:09,599
Lao Er.

911
00:32:09,839 --> 00:32:10,680
Dad, calm down.

912
00:32:48,480 --> 00:32:49,160
Sai Xiuliang!

913
00:32:50,559 --> 00:32:51,680
Second Uncle, Second Aunt!

914
00:32:51,920 --> 00:32:52,519
Dinner isn't even over yet!

915
00:32:52,519 --> 00:32:53,200
What are you doing?

916
00:32:53,200 --> 00:32:54,680
Come set off firecrackers, Second Aunt!

917
00:32:55,079 --> 00:32:56,039
Second Uncle, come set off firecrackers!

918
00:32:56,039 --> 00:32:56,759
Let's go.

919
00:32:57,200 --> 00:32:58,680
Move, move. You still want to go back in?

920
00:32:59,680 --> 00:33:01,400
So your dad can slap you again?

921
00:33:01,599 --> 00:33:02,160
Let's go.

922
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:03,279
Second Uncle, Second Aunt!

923
00:33:03,279 --> 00:33:03,759
Get back inside!

924
00:33:04,799 --> 00:33:05,400
Let's go.

925
00:33:22,279 --> 00:33:22,839
What are you trying to do?

926
00:33:24,039 --> 00:33:25,759
Wen Jiayin, what are you trying to pull?

927
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:26,920
Second Brother quit his job,

928
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:27,599
and he didn't tell Dad.

929
00:33:27,599 --> 00:33:28,920
That's his own business!

930
00:33:29,119 --> 00:33:30,960
Why did you have to light the fuse?!

931
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:32,680
Go play somewhere else!

932
00:33:32,839 --> 00:33:33,680
What are you staring at?

933
00:33:34,240 --> 00:33:34,559
And another thing!

934
00:33:35,279 --> 00:33:35,920
The whole family

935
00:33:36,359 --> 00:33:37,599
finally got together

936
00:33:37,599 --> 00:33:38,720
to have a meal in peace.

937
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:40,359
And you had to cause a scene!

938
00:33:40,599 --> 00:33:41,400
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

939
00:33:41,559 --> 00:33:42,440
Second Brother pushed me!

940
00:33:42,839 --> 00:33:44,160
Third Brother pushed me! Fourth Brother pushed me!

941
00:33:44,160 --> 00:33:45,559
Your whole family pushed me!

942
00:33:45,680 --> 00:33:46,519
Who pushed you?!

943
00:33:46,519 --> 00:33:48,799
I've waited on your Sai family for years!

944
00:33:48,880 --> 00:33:50,880
Tell me, out of everyone in this house,

945
00:33:50,880 --> 00:33:53,200
who hasn't been waited on hand and foot?

946
00:33:53,720 --> 00:33:56,119
Who has ever helped me except Xiaowu?

947
00:33:56,480 --> 00:33:58,400
In the end, I'm the villain!

948
00:33:58,519 --> 00:34:00,680
To hell with being Qingyangli's saintly martyr!

949
00:34:00,920 --> 00:34:02,039
Anyone else can have it!

950
00:34:03,160 --> 00:34:04,920
Even that saintly martyr had people crying!

951
00:34:04,920 --> 00:34:05,759
What do I get?

952
00:34:06,559 --> 00:34:08,800
Second Brother's family acts high and mighty,

953
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:10,199
giving me the cold shoulder!

954
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:13,679
I nursed their mother until she died,

955
00:34:13,719 --> 00:34:15,440
and they don't appreciate me one bit!

956
00:34:16,360 --> 00:34:18,559
They even said they'd give me a banner

957
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:21,000
and interview me!

958
00:34:21,239 --> 00:34:21,679
That's enough!

959
00:34:22,039 --> 00:34:23,440
When they need me,

960
00:34:23,480 --> 00:34:24,519
I'm their sister-in-law.

961
00:34:24,519 --> 00:34:25,880
When they don't,

962
00:34:25,880 --> 00:34:26,920
I'm just that...

963
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:28,400
Alright, that's enough from you!

964
00:34:28,760 --> 00:34:29,719
You've been wronged, alright?

965
00:34:29,719 --> 00:34:30,840
Serving your Sai family,

966
00:34:30,840 --> 00:34:33,000
I am sick and tired of it!

967
00:34:33,679 --> 00:34:34,159
Right,

968
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:35,599
you're the most wronged of all!

969
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:36,360
Happy now?

970
00:34:38,280 --> 00:34:40,199
Enough, enough, enough!

971
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:41,079
Whatever the case,

972
00:34:41,159 --> 00:34:42,039
it's a holiday.

973
00:34:42,079 --> 00:34:43,760
You shouldn't be fueling the fire!

974
00:34:44,320 --> 00:34:45,079
If word gets out,

975
00:34:45,400 --> 00:34:46,039
the neighbors

976
00:34:46,679 --> 00:34:48,320
won't say nice things about you!

977
00:34:48,880 --> 00:34:49,320
Come on.

978
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:50,159
Come on.

979
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:51,440
Let's go.

980
00:34:51,719 --> 00:34:52,119
Move it.

981
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:53,480
Go apologize to Dad.

982
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:55,360
Do as you're told.

983
00:34:55,719 --> 00:34:56,119
I'm not going!

984
00:34:56,199 --> 00:34:56,440
You...

985
00:34:56,960 --> 00:34:58,320
Go apologize to Dad!

986
00:34:58,320 --> 00:34:58,920
I did nothing wrong!

987
00:34:59,599 --> 00:35:00,440
Second Brother is in the wrong!

988
00:35:00,760 --> 00:35:01,960
If anyone should apologize, it's him!

989
00:35:02,239 --> 00:35:03,239
I didn't frame him!

990
00:35:05,559 --> 00:35:06,639
I just let something slip!

991
00:35:06,639 --> 00:35:07,119
Fine, fine, fine!

992
00:35:07,199 --> 00:35:07,719
You did nothing wrong.

993
00:35:08,320 --> 00:35:08,840
You're always right!

994
00:35:08,880 --> 00:35:09,320
Happy now?

995
00:35:09,519 --> 00:35:09,960
I'm the one at fault!

996
00:35:10,360 --> 00:35:11,679
I'll go apologize, alright?

997
00:35:14,800 --> 00:35:15,599
What are you two doing?

998
00:35:16,119 --> 00:35:17,519
Dad, are you and Mom fighting?

999
00:35:18,360 --> 00:35:18,800
Xiaowu,

1000
00:35:19,280 --> 00:35:19,880
take her to do her homework.

1001
00:35:20,079 --> 00:35:20,840
I already told you,

1002
00:35:20,840 --> 00:35:22,280
I finished it long ago!

1003
00:35:22,960 --> 00:35:23,239
You...

1004
00:35:23,559 --> 00:35:24,679
I-I'll have you write it again!

1005
00:35:38,400 --> 00:35:38,679
Dad!

1006
00:35:38,800 --> 00:35:39,119
Dad!

1007
00:35:39,920 --> 00:35:40,239
Dad!

1008
00:36:02,920 --> 00:36:03,559
Brother Xi,

1009
00:36:04,559 --> 00:36:06,159
out for a stroll all by yourself?

1010
00:36:06,840 --> 00:36:07,719
Had a fight at home?

1011
00:36:08,320 --> 00:36:09,559
Over the demolition money, huh?

1012
00:36:10,880 --> 00:36:11,880
Skipping the reunion dinner?

1013
00:36:12,679 --> 00:36:13,199
Stop walking.

1014
00:36:13,320 --> 00:36:13,760
Your son...

1015
00:36:14,119 --> 00:36:15,039
your second son went over that way!

1016
00:36:15,360 --> 00:36:15,719
Over there!

1017
00:36:15,840 --> 00:36:16,960
Reunion dinner my foot!

1018
00:36:17,960 --> 00:36:19,559
People are still working on that site!

1019
00:36:19,920 --> 00:36:20,880
They need to eat, too.

1020
00:36:22,239 --> 00:36:22,679
Qingyou!

1021
00:36:23,159 --> 00:36:24,199
Come out, I need to ask you something.

1022
00:36:24,960 --> 00:36:25,480
What's up?

1023
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:26,320
What do you mean, "What's up?"

1024
00:36:27,159 --> 00:36:29,039
People are still wo- working on that site!

1025
00:36:29,039 --> 00:36:30,519
Instead of k-keeping an eye on them,

1026
00:36:30,519 --> 00:36:31,760
you come over here to mooch a meal?

1027
00:36:32,960 --> 00:36:33,719
It's Mid-Autumn Festival.

1028
00:36:33,719 --> 00:36:34,679
Isn't everyone off today?

1029
00:36:34,840 --> 00:36:35,480
Who still works?

1030
00:36:35,480 --> 00:36:36,039
Says who?

1031
00:36:36,840 --> 00:36:37,800
Who gave them the day off?

1032
00:36:38,239 --> 00:36:38,960
Did you authorize it?

1033
00:36:39,079 --> 00:36:39,639
No, no, no!

1034
00:36:39,960 --> 00:36:40,360
That...

1035
00:36:40,960 --> 00:36:42,000
Down south, down south!

1036
00:36:42,159 --> 00:36:43,039
That site down south,

1037
00:36:43,199 --> 00:36:44,880
several guys are still, still working overtime!

1038
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:46,519
Uncle, you're heading south?

1039
00:36:46,599 --> 00:36:48,159
You two didn't get your stories straight this time.

1040
00:36:48,599 --> 00:36:49,880
Wait, Uncle, let me come with you.

1041
00:36:49,880 --> 00:36:50,519
Why are you going?

1042
00:36:50,960 --> 00:36:52,199
He doesn't even know where he's going.

1043
00:36:52,360 --> 00:36:53,199
Why are you tagging along?

1044
00:36:54,039 --> 00:36:55,360
They definitely had a fight.

1045
00:37:05,639 --> 00:37:06,960
What's Sister-in-law's deal?

1046
00:37:07,719 --> 00:37:09,320
Why did she pick today

1047
00:37:10,320 --> 00:37:11,559
to say all that?

1048
00:37:11,920 --> 00:37:12,679
She did it on purpose, obviously.

1049
00:37:13,159 --> 00:37:13,840
What do you mean?

1050
00:37:15,840 --> 00:37:17,800
To piss Dad off on purpose, right?

1051
00:37:18,199 --> 00:37:20,639
Put all of our Sai family brains together,

1052
00:37:22,480 --> 00:37:23,880
and we're no match for Wen Jiayin alone.

1053
00:37:26,679 --> 00:37:27,400
Sai Xiuhe,

1054
00:37:29,119 --> 00:37:30,559
did you know all along?

1055
00:37:30,639 --> 00:37:32,320
Did you tell Sister-in-law?

1056
00:37:32,519 --> 00:37:32,800
Me?

1057
00:37:33,400 --> 00:37:35,039
I'm the biggest idiot here.

1058
00:37:35,760 --> 00:37:36,840
I'm the one who got sold out

1059
00:37:36,840 --> 00:37:38,239
and helped them count the cash!

1060
00:37:38,599 --> 00:37:40,320
I'm your real sister!

1061
00:37:40,639 --> 00:37:41,519
Why did you tell her first

1062
00:37:41,519 --> 00:37:42,679
instead of telling me?

1063
00:37:42,679 --> 00:37:43,639
What's the point of telling you?

1064
00:37:44,239 --> 00:37:44,880
Tell you? You...

1065
00:37:45,480 --> 00:37:46,280
Mind your own business.

1066
00:37:46,519 --> 00:37:47,360
Sai Xiuhe!

1067
00:37:47,679 --> 00:37:49,159
So you colluded with Sister-in-law

1068
00:37:49,280 --> 00:37:50,599
just for the money,

1069
00:37:50,880 --> 00:37:52,239
specially picked today

1070
00:37:52,320 --> 00:37:54,199
to humiliate Second Brother, didn't you?

1071
00:37:54,320 --> 00:37:55,159
Me, humiliate him?

1072
00:37:55,159 --> 00:37:57,000
Wen Jiayin just used me as a pawn!

1073
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:57,760
Can't you see that?

1074
00:37:57,840 --> 00:37:59,159
Wen Jiayin dug a pit for me.

1075
00:37:59,159 --> 00:38:00,239
With a brain like mine,

1076
00:38:00,320 --> 00:38:01,760
even with eyes in the back of my head,

1077
00:38:01,760 --> 00:38:02,800
I couldn't have seen it coming!

1078
00:38:02,960 --> 00:38:04,039
I jumped right into this trap,

1079
00:38:04,039 --> 00:38:04,719
and Wen Jiayin would still say,

1080
00:38:04,840 --> 00:38:06,079
"Sai Xiuhe, you jumped in yourself."

1081
00:38:07,079 --> 00:38:08,840
If you hadn't handed her the knife,

1082
00:38:08,840 --> 00:38:09,840
could she have stabbed Second Brother?

1083
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:12,079
You two colluded just for the money!

1084
00:38:12,199 --> 00:38:13,360
Now you've driven Dad off in anger.

1085
00:38:13,519 --> 00:38:14,960
Just wait until he comes back to deal with you!

1086
00:38:17,360 --> 00:38:17,920
Let him!

1087
00:38:18,159 --> 00:38:18,679
Deal with me,

1088
00:38:18,800 --> 00:38:19,360
Wen Jiayin,

1089
00:38:19,480 --> 00:38:20,320
and Second Brother—all of us!

1090
00:38:20,559 --> 00:38:21,440
Forget about buying the house too!

1091
00:38:21,599 --> 00:38:22,599
Can we stop talking about money?

1092
00:38:22,760 --> 00:38:23,199
It's so late.

1093
00:38:23,199 --> 00:38:24,039
Dad went out all alone,

1094
00:38:24,199 --> 00:38:24,960
and we don't even know where.

1095
00:38:25,639 --> 00:38:26,400
I'm really worried.

1096
00:38:27,039 --> 00:38:27,440
He'll be fine.

1097
00:38:27,679 --> 00:38:28,639
He could walk around this village

1098
00:38:28,639 --> 00:38:29,639
eight times with his eyes closed.

1099
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:30,639
He's completely safe.

1100
00:38:31,039 --> 00:38:31,559
Besides,

1101
00:38:31,719 --> 00:38:33,199
he was bound to get furious sooner or later.

1102
00:38:33,599 --> 00:38:34,960
That's what he gets for favoring Second Brother.

1103
00:38:37,599 --> 00:38:38,000
Lao Jin,

1104
00:38:39,920 --> 00:38:40,480
what did you mean

1105
00:38:42,760 --> 00:38:43,280
by that today?

1106
00:38:43,800 --> 00:38:44,440
Got an agenda?

1107
00:38:45,079 --> 00:38:46,079
Does what I think even matter?

1108
00:38:46,639 --> 00:38:47,920
I just stated a fact today.

1109
00:38:48,239 --> 00:38:49,119
Qianjin's household registration

1110
00:38:49,559 --> 00:38:50,039
is right here.

1111
00:38:51,920 --> 00:38:53,199
You think everyone is like you,

1112
00:38:54,039 --> 00:38:55,639
obsessing over money, money, money?

1113
00:38:56,079 --> 00:38:58,039
Turns out you're the one we should've guarded against!

1114
00:39:04,239 --> 00:39:04,559
Where's Dad?

1115
00:39:05,159 --> 00:39:05,800
Dad went out.

1116
00:39:06,960 --> 00:39:07,480
Where did he go?

1117
00:39:07,880 --> 00:39:08,199
Don't know.

1118
00:39:10,760 --> 00:39:11,639
Three grown adults here,

1119
00:39:13,079 --> 00:39:13,760
unbelievable.

1120
00:39:21,480 --> 00:39:21,800
Sitting,

1121
00:39:22,360 --> 00:39:23,239
just sitting there waiting.

1122
00:39:23,719 --> 00:39:24,440
Waiting to split the money,

1123
00:39:24,639 --> 00:39:25,880
waiting for Sister-in-law to clean up after you.

1124
00:39:26,280 --> 00:39:26,960
If Sister-in-law doesn't come down,

1125
00:39:27,079 --> 00:39:27,920
nobody lifts a finger, right?

1126
00:39:28,199 --> 00:39:29,000
So in this house,

1127
00:39:29,559 --> 00:39:31,159
you just work your sister-in-law to the bone?

1128
00:39:47,800 --> 00:39:48,199
Does it hurt?

1129
00:39:49,199 --> 00:39:49,679
Much better.

1130
00:39:51,800 --> 00:39:52,480
Feeling any better?

1131
00:39:53,199 --> 00:39:54,280
Much better. Don't worry, Mom.

1132
00:39:54,800 --> 00:39:56,239
Look at your father's temper...

1133
00:39:56,320 --> 00:39:58,079
Even so, he shouldn't be hitting anyone!

1134
00:39:59,519 --> 00:40:00,000
Meifan,

1135
00:40:00,519 --> 00:40:01,159
you too.

1136
00:40:01,480 --> 00:40:02,559
Why didn't you try to stop him?

1137
00:40:02,599 --> 00:40:03,639
How could I stop him?

1138
00:40:04,400 --> 00:40:06,239
Truth is, that slap was meant for me.

1139
00:40:06,719 --> 00:40:07,440
What do you mean?

1140
00:40:08,039 --> 00:40:08,679
His dad thinks

1141
00:40:08,679 --> 00:40:10,280
I must've pushed him to quit his job.

1142
00:40:10,719 --> 00:40:12,840
That I ruined his son's bright future

1143
00:40:12,840 --> 00:40:14,320
and humiliated the Sai family.

1144
00:40:14,719 --> 00:40:16,519
I don't care what others think of me,

1145
00:40:17,199 --> 00:40:19,360
but don't hit my husband in front of me!

1146
00:40:19,440 --> 00:40:20,519
With so many people watching, no less!

1147
00:40:23,400 --> 00:40:23,760
Xiuliang,

1148
00:40:24,519 --> 00:40:25,599
now that you've walked out,

1149
00:40:25,679 --> 00:40:26,800
is your dad all right?

1150
00:40:27,880 --> 00:40:28,159
Dad!

1151
00:40:28,840 --> 00:40:30,360
Did you even hear what I just said?

1152
00:40:31,039 --> 00:40:32,079
I heard you. I'm not deaf.

1153
00:40:32,480 --> 00:40:33,519
Then why are you still worrying about his dad?

1154
00:40:34,360 --> 00:40:36,360
Your father-in-law beat my son-in-law like this.

1155
00:40:36,440 --> 00:40:37,400
You think you're the only one heartbroken?

1156
00:40:37,400 --> 00:40:38,159
You think it doesn't hurt me?

1157
00:40:38,800 --> 00:40:39,440
Honestly!

1158
00:40:40,920 --> 00:40:41,679
Your father-in-law hitting him

1159
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:42,679
was wrong.

1160
00:40:43,679 --> 00:40:44,159
But Xiuliang,

1161
00:40:45,000 --> 00:40:46,079
then again,

1162
00:40:46,719 --> 00:40:47,760
who else was he supposed to hit?

1163
00:40:48,800 --> 00:40:51,159
Though the slap landed on your face,

1164
00:40:51,320 --> 00:40:52,159
I think

1165
00:40:52,800 --> 00:40:53,960
the one hurting the most right now

1166
00:40:55,039 --> 00:40:55,880
must be him.

1167
00:41:03,400 --> 00:41:06,400
Look at him carrying that Port Authority bag every day,

1168
00:41:06,679 --> 00:41:08,320
drinking from that Port Authority mug.

1169
00:41:08,480 --> 00:41:08,840
Why?

1170
00:41:09,360 --> 00:41:10,559
Because he cares about this.

1171
00:41:11,360 --> 00:41:12,360
Since ancient times,

1172
00:41:12,559 --> 00:41:13,719
"A good scholar becomes an official."

1173
00:41:13,719 --> 00:41:15,119
That belief is etched into his bones.

1174
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:16,440
A man like him,

1175
00:41:16,679 --> 00:41:17,559
who's weathered storms

1176
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:19,320
and crawled out of the mud...

1177
00:41:19,360 --> 00:41:20,679
A tenured public post,

1178
00:41:20,840 --> 00:41:22,719
carries immense weight in his heart.

1179
00:41:22,920 --> 00:41:25,559
It's not just about having an iron rice bowl.

1180
00:41:25,880 --> 00:41:26,760
To him,

1181
00:41:26,760 --> 00:41:28,239
it represents total

1182
00:41:28,639 --> 00:41:30,719
security and dignity.

1183
00:41:31,440 --> 00:41:32,119
Even if he cares that much,

1184
00:41:32,119 --> 00:41:33,360
he still shouldn't treat Xiuliang like this!

1185
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:33,960
Meifan,

1186
00:41:34,320 --> 00:41:36,280
you need to see it from his perspective.

1187
00:41:36,599 --> 00:41:37,199
But Xiuliang,

1188
00:41:37,639 --> 00:41:38,280
when it comes to this,

1189
00:41:38,360 --> 00:41:39,719
whether your dad approves or not,

1190
00:41:40,079 --> 00:41:41,119
there's no turning back for you now.

1191
00:41:41,480 --> 00:41:43,440
What you need to do now is stay focused

1192
00:41:43,679 --> 00:41:45,239
and get this venture off the ground.

1193
00:41:45,719 --> 00:41:46,639
Once you reach the point

1194
00:41:46,639 --> 00:41:48,000
where your father can truly

1195
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:49,159
see tangible results,

1196
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:50,480
you won't need to say a word.

1197
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:51,840
He'll understand on his own.

1198
00:42:28,159 --> 00:42:29,559
How's the renovation of the law firm going?

1199
00:42:29,760 --> 00:42:30,519
It's moving pretty fast.

1200
00:42:31,320 --> 00:42:32,559
Ready to open next month, right?

1201
00:42:34,079 --> 00:42:34,719
What about projects?

1202
00:42:35,480 --> 00:42:36,760
Any deals in the works?

1203
00:42:37,199 --> 00:42:38,480
You don't want to open

1204
00:42:38,480 --> 00:42:39,280
only to sit around with nothing to do.

1205
00:42:39,280 --> 00:42:40,320
That's a rough spot to be in.

1206
00:42:41,199 --> 00:42:43,199
We're in talks with Tengyue Real Estate right now.

1207
00:42:43,639 --> 00:42:45,599
Discussing outsourcing some of their legal work.

1208
00:42:46,199 --> 00:42:46,480
Well,

1209
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:49,880
Tengyue Group is a major, powerful company.

1210
00:42:50,159 --> 00:42:51,679
Congratulations are in order, aren't they?

1211
00:42:52,480 --> 00:42:53,719
So when are you signing the contract?

1212
00:42:54,639 --> 00:42:56,000
He's cautious.

1213
00:42:56,360 --> 00:42:57,440
He wants to wait until his resignation goes through

1214
00:42:58,039 --> 00:42:58,480
before signing.

1215
00:42:58,760 --> 00:42:59,960
Either way, waiting while negotiating

1216
00:42:59,960 --> 00:43:00,480
doesn't conflict at all.

1217
00:43:00,639 --> 00:43:01,039
Good, good, good.

1218
00:43:01,039 --> 00:43:01,320
Right.

1219
00:43:01,440 --> 00:43:01,920
Xiuliang,

1220
00:43:02,320 --> 00:43:04,199
you're in the prime of your career.

1221
00:43:04,320 --> 00:43:05,480
Be a bit bolder.

1222
00:43:05,599 --> 00:43:07,199
Make a real name for yourself.

1223
00:43:07,800 --> 00:43:08,119
Right, definitely.

1224
00:43:08,119 --> 00:43:10,079
I think this is a rare opportunity too.

1225
00:43:10,239 --> 00:43:10,880
Don't worry, both of you.

1226
00:43:20,119 --> 00:43:21,159
Dad gave me the ledger.

1227
00:43:21,280 --> 00:43:21,960
Still mad at me?

1228
00:43:22,360 --> 00:43:23,039
What are you doing?

1229
00:43:23,320 --> 00:43:24,440
Helping you check the accounts.

1230
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:26,000
What are you checking?

1231
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:27,000
Don't... Don't look!

1232
00:43:27,079 --> 00:43:28,400
Dad said this ledger

1233
00:43:28,559 --> 00:43:29,519
is for my eyes only.

1234
00:43:29,920 --> 00:43:31,760
What did we talk about in the restroom?

1235
00:43:31,880 --> 00:43:32,920
Let me jog your memory.

1236
00:43:33,400 --> 00:43:34,480
When you were talking to me,

1237
00:43:34,480 --> 00:43:35,960
you hadn't resigned from the Port Authority yet.

1238
00:43:36,119 --> 00:43:37,320
What kind of violation is that?

1239
00:43:37,320 --> 00:43:38,199
You should know very well.

1240
00:43:38,320 --> 00:43:39,000
What if one day,

1241
00:43:39,000 --> 00:43:40,679
someone bursts into my office with a tape,

1242
00:43:40,679 --> 00:43:42,000
sits right where you're sitting,

1243
00:43:43,360 --> 00:43:43,960
and threatens me?
